From 1ab525591fe86fe53675dcc8a28acb55e6323a44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpv_tc <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:47:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] decklink: optionally delay audio by the output latency

--decklink-audio-sync adds the mirror's latency (new decklink-latency
property) to the effective audio delay, so that the computer's audio
matches the DeckLink output instead of the window. --audio-delay stays
the user's own correction on top. The latency is picked up in the
playloop once the output runs. The DeckLink menu gets a 'Sync audio to
DeckLink' toggle, saved with the device in ~~/decklink.state.
